# Secrets. Never committed, in any form.
#
# There is no git repository in this working copy yet — this file exists so that the
# first `git init && git add .` cannot publish a credential. The patterns below are the
# ones that matter for this project specifically: the environment file, the arbiter's
# databases, TLS material, and the build-request spool (which holds requester
# correspondence and is the only place personal data is written to disk).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# `.infisical.json` is deliberately NOT ignored: `infisical init` writes the local project
# link there, it contains no secret, and the team is meant to commit it. The values it
# points at live in Infisical, not in this repository.

# Operator overrides that a deployment may drop in beside the code.
*.local
*.local.*

# TLS material, if a certificate is ever placed here for direct HTTPS.
certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx

# Runtime state: SQLite databases and their journals, plus the WAL sidecars.
.zeus-data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# The build-request spool and every process log. Logs may contain operator tokens and
# requester addresses; they are artefacts of a running process, not source.
.zeus-requests.log
.zeus-*.log
*.log

# Upload quarantine. Anything a user sent us lands here and must never be published.
uploads/
quarantine/

# Build output and dependency caches.
dist/
node_modules/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local agent runtime state.
.freebuff/
